[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and closed on 5 October. Read the bodies,
not the subjects, and it held three problems. Engineering fixed the parser and retired the
booking-v3 form. The third problem is still open.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but one-day moves still have no fix. New reports of a date one day off go to
the open ticket below, not to #4471.
</Callout>

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the booked date and the date we sent are the same two numbers, day and month
  swapped (7 April → 4 July). It happened to every tenant that writes the day first, through
  any channel. Fixed.
- **`hint`**: the same swap, but only through the **booking form** of tenants on `booking-v3`.
  That form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people typed the month first, and the
  form then read it day first. The parser fix never reached it. The form is retired.
  [#4471's own table](/kb/incidents/4471) already showed it as *no ticket of its own*.
- **`one-day`**: the date lands one day off, not swapped: Tuesday became Monday, a meeting fell
  on different days in Lisbon and Toronto, *only June*, an invite older than its booking. No
  day/month swap gives a one-day move, so neither fix touches it. It points to a timezone
  conversion. The desk read these the same way (`desk-notes.json`) and files them under `parser`
  by tenant, so they are counted there too.

## Why one ticket hid them

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. "Wrong day"
  reads the same whatever the cause.
- Intake tags come from the reporter's browser, not the tenant, and disagree with the cause on
  dozens of these reports. Count by tenant and channel, then read the bodies.
- The export repeats some reports. Count unique ids.

